r/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5e7de2-2dc0-5fd1-b9b6-4c9adab8f1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286000} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e3e65d8-f16e-521d-b9f5-3912eedae649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4dfd88c-8fd0-5fa6-a390-4f040e6c68f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-344578" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/ca5e8035505f20619b6707d6d1f2d0b7b2f125a004a0dbd9d448840b0e4ffd99.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\sqrt{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
